00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:42.310
No sense waiting for what won't come.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.150
What are you smiling for?

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:50.780
Come with me today.
There's somewhere I want to go.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:53.620
You know the deal.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:57.790
Each area of the Underground
is walled off.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:58.950
So?

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.080
So, we can't go where we want.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.920
I think the one by Tower Records is open.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.210
Who knows when we'll get a mission.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:13.680
Why not ignore it?
Someone else will finish it for us.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.890
I have to win this game.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:22.480
Your entry fee, the thing that
currently matters most to you...

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.400
...is Shiki Misaki.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.150
I got Shiki into this mess.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:31.860
To bring Shiki back to life,

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:35.570
I have to win this game, no matter what.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:39.410
I have to do the missions myself.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.170
Are you even listening?

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.630
I am.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:48.090
Calm down.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:53.930
It's here!

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.010
Go to Cat Street

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.010
You have 15 minutes

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.010
Incompletes will be erased

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.720
Reach Cat Street in 15 minutes?!

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.640
We've gotta run!

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:05.020
Hey! Where are you?!

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.190
Right here.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:08.400
Let's run!

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.070
"The World Ends With You The Animation"

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.160
Cat Street

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.330
Did we... make it?

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.550
Run faster.

00:03:56.550 --> 00:04:00.090
I hate getting tired out.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.760
Neku, that's the place.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:03.970
Huh?

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.850
Wildkat. That's where I wanted to go.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:12.150
I recommend the coffee and pancakes.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.150
And the donuts aren't bad.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.280
That mission was...

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:20.490
A fake I sent you.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:24.910
It worked even better than I imagined.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.330
Be serious!

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:27.960
This is important.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.710
For you too, Neku.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.040
Mr. Hanekoma.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:36.300
Hey there! I've been waiting, Joshua.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.170
Mr. Hanekoma?!

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:41.840
Hey! You're playing the game <i>again</i>?!

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.850
So, the girl got to come back to life?

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:51.230
Shiki... became my entry fee.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.770
It's my fault.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.280
That so?

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.610
Don't cry over spilled milk.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:01.990
Wait a sec.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:07.120
You're friendly with Mr. Hanekoma, Neku.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:11.250
Not really. He helped me out a bunch.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:14.000
He's been helping me for a long time too.

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:16.630
How long?

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:21.010
You see, I could see things
that others can't.

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:24.510
Reapers, Noise, Players,

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:27.560
and even you, Neku.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.520
Since when?

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.270
I forget.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:35.020
Anyway, the Reapers' Game intrigued me.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:39.360
There's one other person
like me in Shibuya.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:40.650
Mr. Hanekoma?

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:43.200
Right. He helped Players that Reapers tricked

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:47.330
or tried to make self-destruct
using cowardly traps.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:55.000
And once I started coming here,
things got more fun.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:59.170
There're only dead people in
the Underground! How is that fun?

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:01.550
It is.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:04.970
We risk our lives and desperately
race around Shibuya.

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:09.260
You won't find recreation this
stimulating in the Realground.

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:13.600
You <i>volunteered </i>for the Reapers' Game?

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:18.730
A place that never changes
might as well be dead.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.490
I don't need that.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:25.610
Maybe you don't, but I'm different.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:28.620
I don't even know why I died.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:31.750
I'll do what I want, how I want,
as much as I want.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:35.540
I...

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.010
Here you go.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:45.970
I'm proud of this coffee.

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:49.680
Thanks.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.390
Hot!

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.230
Be careful.

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:01.780
Want a donut too? They're good.

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:03.860
No thanks.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.900
More importantly, it's ready, right?

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:07.910
You bet. Give me your phones.

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:11.200
You too, Neku.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.500
What do you need my phone for?

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.830
To add a new feature.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.880
I asked for these before I
came to the Underground.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:22.000
It's been a long wait.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.090
Think of the guy who has to rush for you.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.550
So, the person you've been calling...

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.930
Is Mr. Hanekoma.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:36.230
Have I been too suspicious of this guy?

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:39.730
Hey, what were you talking about just now?

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:45.740
He said he saw the Underground from the
Realground and came here on purpose.

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:49.990
He comes to talk about that
stuff people won't understand.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:55.700
My café's got Reaper approval,
so it's good for that kind of talk.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.540
That's quite enough.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:03.710
Well, you're partners. Try to get along.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.670
Whoops, I messed that up.

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:09.340
Is it all right?

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:12.300
I'm supremely talented,

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:17.270
but messing with the Underground
from the Realground isn't easy.

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:19.350
Is it that hard?

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:22.820
I can't do my best work.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:24.360
There.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.690
I installed the apps you wanted.

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:31.870
Thank you. Now we can start searching.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:33.700
Searching for what?

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.620
I'll tell you when we find it.

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:37.830
Seriously?

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:41.130
It's not worth getting
riled up at him every time.

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:43.290
Enjoy every moment with all you've got!

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:44.920
Those words!

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.590
What's up now?

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:48.670
Nothing.

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:53.600
CAT, someone I respect,
says the same thing.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:56.640
You know the graffiti in Udagawa?

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:59.020
Yeah, it's famous.

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:01.690
That's some of CAT's best work.

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:04.940
CAT's multi-talented.
They can do anything.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:07.480
Shibuya's full of CAT's designs.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:10.900
You could say CAT's very existence is art.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.370
Sounds like a big influence on you.

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:15.490
Anyhow,

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:19.370
the world ends with you.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:25.090
If you want to enjoy life,
keep expanding your horizons.

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:30.840
This place is a melting pot of all
kinds of emotions, good and bad.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:37.060
Things might be tough now, but hold
on to the last thing left inside you.

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:40.100
I bet it'll change you.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:44.230
What if it changes parts
of him that it shouldn't?

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:47.690
I still believe in possibilities.

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:52.110
Any change on your end?

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.320
Not yet.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:57.080
I'll just step outside.

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:01.330
You put it on my phone too?

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:03.170
That and a camera app.

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:07.290
You never know what missions
you'll get. Best to be prepared.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:10.210
Oh yeah, we didn't get a mission today.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:14.640
Yeah? Well, that's the Game Master's job.

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:19.520
This Minamimoto character
is unpredictable and cruel.

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:21.270
Watch out.

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:22.810
Neku, come here!

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:24.190
I got a hit!

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.150
A hit on what?

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:33.530
It's made to detect
high-energy signatures.

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:36.280
Is that what you're looking for?

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.490
I hope so.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:42.370
I'm detecting them in Udagawa
and Scramble Crossing.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.620
Udagawa's closer.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.790
No, we'll hit Scramble Crossing first.

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:50.960
The size of this signature's a bit odd.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.270
Red Skull pins.

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:06.600
It looks like everyone
here is wearing them.

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:10.400
Red Skull pins!

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:22.240
The signatures are moving
in sync with the pedestrians.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.830
Is it picking up the Red Skull pins?

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:26.750
They sure are popular.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:30.840
CAT's designs really are something.

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:34.010
They look like Player pins.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:39.680
Player pins are designed and
controlled by the Composer.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:42.260
The Composer? The Reapers' boss?

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:46.140
The Composer is above the Reapers.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:49.190
They're capable of erasing this dimension.

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:52.270
Then... is CAT the Composer?

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:55.190
I wonder.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:59.870
Was it the one in Udagawa?

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:01.870
What are you trying to do?

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:06.040
I want to properly guide Shibuya.

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:12.500
You'll come to want to help me.

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:36.610
Wha--?! Another went by?

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:38.030
Looks like it.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:45.910
You won't wait for a mission?

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:48.540
If we get one, it comes first.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:49.670
Where to?

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:52.630
Udagawa. We missed it yesterday.

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:54.630
Now you're getting it.

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:57.800
I don't want to "get" anything. I just...

00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:01.760
If I go there, I might
find out why I died.

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:10.100
Fourteen Players were confirmed
erased as of yesterday.

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:15.440
Minamimoto's not half bad.
This game might end before the final day.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:20.530
But no missions have been
issued yesterday or today.

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:24.700
Then why are there fewer Players?
Where's Minamimoto?

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.080
Missing since yesterday,

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:30.210
but his "art" has been
sighted in various locations.

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:34.790
He's in the Underground?

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:36.090
Most likely.

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:42.300
He hates being part of a crowd.
Leave him be for a little while.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:44.090
As you wish.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.970
Any other issues?

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:50.390
Reapers across Shibuya have come
under attack from Taboo Noise.

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:56.770
So, that's what's erasing Players.
How does it affect our forces?

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.280
Not an issue.

00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:02.150
I've already begun identifying
and locating the culprit.

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:05.950
I'm also investigating potential
links between incidents.

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:10.540
In that case, Konishi, it's in your hands.

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:13.120
Understood, sir.

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:20.760
Sho Minamimoto.

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:23.590
His numbers are second
only to Mr. Kitaniji's,

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:27.100
and he's easily the youngest
officer in Reaper history.

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:29.310
A true genius.

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:32.140
What on earth is he after?

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:38.230
The wall's closed.

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:40.030
Shall we look for an open one?

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:42.950
What?! Are you kidding me?

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:45.030
That's no ordinary mic!

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:48.330
It's Death March's heart and soul!

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:51.250
I'm telling you,
just report it to the cops.

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:53.540
No way! How would that look?

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:56.040
We're metal and Reapers.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:15:00.170
But we've looked everywhere
and still can't find it.

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:01.760
We can use this.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.340
What now?

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:09.180
We'll find that mic for you.

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:12.060
D-Don't just decide these things!

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:16.020
In exchange, we just want you
to open that wall for us.

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:18.400
Not a bad deal, wouldn't you say?

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:28.120
What do we do, Sota?!

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:31.990
There's nothing we <i>can </i>do!
We're in way over our heads!

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:35.620
What the hell?!
No one told me about a mission!

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:37.830
Taboo Noise?

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:40.250
Nao, let's run for it!

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:42.340
Don't let your guard down.

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:44.380
What are you talking about?

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:46.220
Noise don't attack Re--

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:54.850
You know, you're a real handful.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:59.650
I can take care of myself!

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:15.500
And that was the last time I saw it.

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:16.910
You just forgot it.

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:18.170
I did not!

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:21.840
Maybe someone brought it
to the police as a lost item?

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:25.920
Not quite, it appears.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:27.090
Look.

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:30.590
This mic's zetta sexy!

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:33.470
It'll make a perfect addition to my art!

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:36.770
Minamimoto took it?

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:38.690
And added it to that trash heap?

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:42.230
We can't risk touching it.
He'll kill us if we piss him off.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:46.650
But you know who's responsible,
so will you let us through now?

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:47.990
F-Fine.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:58.960
Isn't it great it came in handy so soon?

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:00.920
A camera that shoots the past?

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:03.540
Mr. Hanekoma's a bigger
deal than I thought.

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:06.880
Although I'm sad to say
it drains a lot of battery.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:10.430
Two shots a day is the limit.
There's room for improve--

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:14.010
This is the strongest signature yet.

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:14.930
Hey!

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:16.470
You're Players, yeah?!

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:17.560
Huh? Yeah.

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:20.270
That place is bad news!
Better steer clear!

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:22.060
Bad how?

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:25.650
There's, like, a ton of weird,
black Noise, plus Reapers showed up.

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:27.110
We ran like hell!

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:29.320
I'm Sota. She's Nao.

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:31.570
Call me Nao-<i>rin</i>, 'K?

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:34.780
I'm Joshua. This is Neku.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:38.080
Everybody else with us got wiped out.

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:39.750
Yeah?

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:43.380
Hey, don't go there, man!

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:46.300
It's pointless, yeah?
There's not even a mission.

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:49.340
Let's all win this thing
and come back to life!

00:17:49.340 --> 00:17:51.760
Don't you know?

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:54.220
We don't all necessarily get to come back.

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:55.640
Hey.

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:57.180
What?

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:59.890
Your partner's also a rival.

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:03.440
So, like, if we win, and one
of us comes back to life,

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:05.480
what happens to the other one?

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:09.530
They just play again, like Neku here.

00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:11.990
You've played before, Nekky?

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:13.360
Yeah.

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:15.870
So, your partner came back, yeah?

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:18.910
No, she didn't.

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:21.290
Because I decided to play,

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:22.540
she was taken as my entry fee.

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:23.460
Wha--?

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:26.000
For real?

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:28.090
In the end, it's my fault.

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:31.380
Sota.

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:34.090
Sorry, we've gotta go.

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.550
Don't overdo it!

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:39.060
What now?

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:52.360
What's with that Noise?!

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:57.780
Things must be bad if Reapers
are getting attacked.

00:18:57.780 --> 00:19:01.750
They're fighting the big one.
Now's our chance to sneak through.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:08.000
I doubt they'll make it that easy.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:17.590
Take 'em down!

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:25.640
Below!

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:26.940
I won't make it!

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:33.900
You OK?!

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:35.320
Ow...

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:38.530
That's a risky way to fight, Neku.

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.870
Don't you want to win?

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:45.660
Yeah.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:49.500
It's slow, but one hit and you're toast.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:52.920
On the other hand,
it can't dodge ranged attacks.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:01.930
It doesn't go down easy.

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:04.180
It's in a different weight class.

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:07.480
This calls for a joint attack.

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:10.060
Its attacks are powerful.

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:12.360
We can't afford to get hit at all.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:16.030
Concentrate, Neku.

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:18.240
I'm through worrying.

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:21.160
If I want to win,
I've gotta trust my partner.

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:26.710
I'll erase them all!

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:50.230
Looks like Phones and Pretty Boy
managed to pull it off.

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:52.190
Like I care!

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:56.530
Anyway, we've got to report to Konishi.

00:20:56.530 --> 00:21:00.530
I can't keep up with all
these irregular missions.

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:03.200
What a waste of effort.

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:05.860
Udagawa

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:13.250
That's some great graffiti.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:16.090
Yeah, it's by CAT.

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:18.920
This is my favorite place.

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:21.800
And it's where I saw myself lying...

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:24.560
...when I scanned him.

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:27.140
What did he...?

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:32.560
What's wrong, Neku? You stopped moving.

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:35.360
Nothing much.

00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:37.440
Just like back then.

00:21:39.490 --> 00:21:41.160
Back then?

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:43.030
When do you mean?!

00:22:16.150 --> 00:22:17.780
This is where I...

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:27.280
He... killed me.

00:23:58.910 --> 00:24:01.920
Turf

00:23:59.540 --> 00:24:01.670
Next time: "Turf."
